<task id="022" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>`sendCommunication()` refinements — `SendCommunicationError` + canonical `attachmentDriveItemIds`</title>
    <phase>Wave 2 — Client: composer engine + wrappers</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>3</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>006</dependencies>
    <blocks>060</blocks>
    <tags>frontend, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies the single typed client gateway (`communicationApi.ts`) that every send-email path depends on; introduces a new exported error class (uniform error contract replacing 3 divergent shapes) + canonical attachment field; ProblemDetails parsing per ADR-019; the changed file is a contract for the entire send-side surface. FULL.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Client-only TypeScript in `communicationApi.ts`; disjoint from the W1/W3 server track. Additive to a file the engine (020) imports — sequence it before or alongside 020's `send()` wiring. No cross-track shared files.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-13</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Refine `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/communicationApi.ts` to land the client half of the FR-06 DTO rename + the uniform error contract (FR-13):
    (a) Add `attachmentDriveItemIds?: string[]` as the canonical attachment field on the request type — TSDoc: "Microsoft Graph `driveItem` IDs (NOT `sprk_document` GUIDs). Canonical per ADR-045."
    (b) Mark `attachmentDocumentIds?: string[]` `@deprecated Use attachmentDriveItemIds. Removed in a future release.` — fires a `console.warn` ONCE per session (module-level flag, not per call) when populated.
    (c) Add exported class `SendCommunicationError extends Error` with readonly `status`, `code`, `detail`, `correlationId`, parsed from the BFF's ProblemDetails (ADR-019) response — with a static `async fromResponse(response): Promise&lt;SendCommunicationError&gt;` that parses `{ type, title, status, detail, instance|traceId, correlationId? }` and falls back to a minimal error (status only) on non-JSON.
    (d) `sendCommunication()` MUST throw `SendCommunicationError` on any non-2xx response (replaces the current thrown `Error`).
    (e) Update docstrings on the request type + `sendCommunication()` to call out driveItem semantics, the throw of `SendCommunicationError`, and the deprecation.

    Empirical Finding #2 (R4 CLAUDE.md): the file HAS `sendCommunication()` but is MISSING both `SendCommunicationError` and `attachmentDriveItemIds`. This is ADDITIVE — no breaking change to existing callers. Callers may still populate BOTH `attachmentDriveItemIds` and `attachmentDocumentIds`; do NOT drop/rename either client-side — the BFF mapping (task 006) resolves precedence server-side (canonical wins, alias logs a deprecation warning).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke shared-library engineer, authoritative on the `@spaarke/ui-components` `services/` layer and the auth-decoupling boundary (injected `authenticatedFetch`, no `@spaarke/auth` import). Familiar with ADR-019 ProblemDetails and ADR-028.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `communicationApi.ts` exports `SendCommunicationError` (`status`/`code`/`detail`/`correlationId`) and accepts both `attachmentDriveItemIds` (canonical) + `attachmentDocumentIds` (deprecated, one-shot warn). `sendCommunication()` throws `SendCommunicationError` on non-2xx. Existing callers compile + send unchanged. No `@spaarke/auth` import. `npm run build:prod` + `npm run lint` clean; downstream-caller audit records no broken contract.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      `communicationApi.ts` is the single typed gateway between every Spaarke client surface and BFF `POST /api/communications/send`. FR-13's "one typed error path" hinges here: `SendCommunicationError` replaces the 3 inconsistent patterns (throw `Error` / return `{success, warning}` / push to `warnings[]`) the assessment found. The engine (task 020) imports `SendCommunicationError` and calls `sendCommunication()` from its `send()` handle.

      BFF side (task 006, W0): `SendCommunicationRequest` gains `AttachmentDriveItemIds` (canonical) + `[Obsolete]` alias `AttachmentDocumentIds`; server normalizes both (canonical wins, alias logs a warning). This client task is the symmetric half. The `attachmentDriveItemIds` values come from `wizardContext.uploadedFiles[].driveItemId`; `DocumentEmailWizard.tsx:494`'s bug (shipping `sprk_document` GUIDs into the deprecated field) is fixed in W6 task 060.

      Auth boundary (ADR-028): shared-lib code MUST NOT import `@spaarke/auth`. `authenticatedFetch` is a parameter. Preserve this.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/communicationApi.ts (UPDATE)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/__tests__/ (unit tests land in task 023)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-13 is binding: `SendCommunicationError` + canonical `attachmentDriveItemIds`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Additive / non-breaking — existing callers using `attachmentDocumentIds` continue to send successfully; both fields may be sent (BFF task 006 resolves precedence).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Parse ProblemDetails `{ type, title, status, detail, instance|traceId, correlationId? }`; fall back to a minimal error on non-JSON.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">`@spaarke/auth` MUST NOT be imported; `authenticatedFetch` injected via parameter (existing pattern).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Deprecation warning fires ONCE per session (module-level flag), not per call.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">TSDoc explicitly states "Microsoft Graph `driveItem` IDs (NOT `sprk_document` GUIDs)."</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Aligns with the R4 Communication ADR canonical send pattern (authored in task 005).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Client-only — no BFF publish-size / CVE obligation.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/spec.md</file>
