  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `communicationApi.ts` end-to-end. Identify the request type, `sendCommunication()` shape, and current non-2xx handling (per empirical finding, a thrown `Error` — confirm). Read `reference/r3-send-side-design.md` §6 for the target shapes.</step>
    <step order="2">Author `SendCommunicationError extends Error` in the same file: readonly `status`, `code?`, `detail?`, `correlationId?`; `name = 'SendCommunicationError'`; static `async fromResponse(response): Promise&lt;SendCommunicationError&gt;` (ProblemDetails parse + fallback).</step>
    <step order="3">Add `attachmentDriveItemIds?: string[]` to the request type with driveItem-semantics TSDoc. Mark `attachmentDocumentIds?: string[]` `@deprecated`.</step>
    <step order="4">Add module-level `let _deprecationWarned = false;`. In `sendCommunication()` after destructure: if `attachmentDocumentIds !== undefined &amp;&amp; !_deprecationWarned` → `console.warn('[Spaarke] attachmentDocumentIds is deprecated. Use attachmentDriveItemIds (ADR-045).')` + set flag.</step>
    <step order="5">In `sendCommunication()`: after `authenticatedFetch(...)`, if `!response.ok` → `throw await SendCommunicationError.fromResponse(response);`. Confirm both fields flow through to the request body when populated (no client-side drop/rename).</step>
    <step order="6">Update docstrings on the request type + `sendCommunication()` (driveItem semantics, error throw, deprecation).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `npm run build:prod` + `npm run lint` in `@spaarke/ui-components` — clean.</step>
    <step order="8">Downstream-caller audit: `Grep` for `sendCommunication` / `communicationApi` in `src/`. Skim each call site to confirm (a) no caller depends on a specific error MESSAGE string (message is informative, not contractual), (b) `instanceof Error` checks still pass (subclass), (c) no caller breaks from the additive field. Record findings in task notes.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: invoke `code-review` on the diff; invoke `adr-check` against ADR-019, ADR-028, ADR-045 + `spec.md`. Address Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark 022 ✅; confirm 060 dependency satisfied.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `current-task.md` per task-execute protocol: status → completed; advance to next pending W2 task.</step>
  </steps>

