    <criterion testable="true">`SendCommunicationError` exported with `status`, `code`, `detail`, `correlationId`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`SendCommunicationError.fromResponse(response)` parses ProblemDetails and returns a populated instance (fallback on non-JSON).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Request type has `attachmentDriveItemIds?: string[]` with driveItem-semantics TSDoc.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Request type still has `attachmentDocumentIds?: string[]` marked `@deprecated`; deprecation warn fires exactly once per session.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`sendCommunication()` throws `SendCommunicationError` on non-2xx.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`@spaarke/auth` is NOT imported in this file (NFR-03 / ADR-028).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` + `npm run lint` clean; downstream-caller audit confirms no broken contract.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Unit tests for `SendCommunicationError` parsing + one-shot deprecation warn land in task 023 (this task implements; 023 verifies). The `code` field maps to ProblemDetails extensions (e.g. `ATTACHMENT_TOO_LARGE`); leave nullable if the BFF does not always populate it. Engine (task 020) imports `SendCommunicationError` from here — do not define it twice.
